{"name":"International Orange","hex":"#ba160c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"international orange","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reddish-orange colour used to set things apart from their surroundings, especially in the aerospace industry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/international_orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"International orange","blocks":[{"text":"International orange is a color used in the aerospace industry and maritime industry to set objects apart from their surroundings, similar to safety orange, but deeper and with a more reddish tone."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_orange","wikidata":"Q2529373"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Launch_entry_suit.jpg/500px-Launch_entry_suit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Launch_entry_suit.jpg/1280px-Launch_entry_suit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Launch_entry_suit.jpg/500px-Launch_entry_suit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The NASA Launch Entry Su